                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c2b7baa8-ef82-3030-9d1b-ea689d92fd24",
                                        "entry_id": "a8a531b2-1bf9-38f2-9a26-792765c99c09",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Initialism of personal computer.",
                                            "A personal computer, especially one similar to an IBM PC that runs Microsoft Windows (or, originally, DOS), usually as opposed to (say) an Apple Mac."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e7cf8b4e-b1e7-4b53-8809-dd191a89f6f0",
                                                "sense_id": "c2b7baa8-ef82-3030-9d1b-ea689d92fd24",
                                                "text": "“For some of the imaging we do,” says Richard Miner, research manager at the University of Lowell's Center for Productivity Enhancement, “we are using both the Amiga and the PC [with the bridge card]. […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ee2d0408-b94e-49c6-92b7-435350dcca2c",
                                                "sense_id": "c2b7baa8-ef82-3030-9d1b-ea689d92fd24",
                                                "text": "In general, the prices for PC and Mac laptops can be competitive, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff7eab78-c373-442c-b6cc-bb86dd9e153a",
                                                "sense_id": "c2b7baa8-ef82-3030-9d1b-ea689d92fd24",
                                                "text": "Versions of Word for PC and Mac",
                                                "translation": "It is not unusual to find both Mac and PC computers in college computer laboratories, so you may need to become familiar with both Word for PCs and Word for Mac.",
                                                "english": "It is not unusual to find both Mac and PC computers in college computer laboratories, so you may need to become familiar with both Word for PCs and Word for Mac."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8d126f3d-97db-49bf-96d9-bc73fb8fc2cc",
                                                "sense_id": "c2b7baa8-ef82-3030-9d1b-ea689d92fd24",
                                                "text": "There’s a devastating narrative being told about the PC these days: It’s dying.\nIt’s not a slow death either. Sales of traditional PCs are collapsing faster than anyone expected."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "254f5435-df4a-418b-aab6-c26f6796ff6b",
                                                "sense_id": "c2b7baa8-ef82-3030-9d1b-ea689d92fd24",
                                                "text": "Looking for the best RAM for your PC in 2023 has gotten a little bit more complicated than before. With the advent of DDR5, you can now choose between a newer standard, and an older one. DDR4 has a differently keyed connector, and you’re also going to have to check that the RAM is compatible with your CPU in the first place. So, what should you buy?"
                                            }
                                        ]
